# Custody service configuration. COPY TO .env AND FILL IN — never commit .env.
#
# The BitGo access token is a BEARER CREDENTIAL: anything holding it can read
# the account. Keep it in the environment or a root-only file on the host, not
# in this repository and not in shell history (prefix commands with a space, or
# load it from a file).

# REQUIRED. The token itself. No default, deliberately.
BITGO_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# "test" (default) or "prod". MUST be set to prod deliberately — a missing or
# misspelled value resolves to the TEST environment, never to the one holding
# real customer funds.
BITGO_ENV=test

# Optional. Set once more than one enterprise exists on the account, otherwise
# balances from an unrelated enterprise are summed in and overstate holdings.
BITGO_ENTERPRISE=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OBSERVED BEHAVIOUR, 2026-11-23 — read this before debugging a 401.
#
# BitGo returns HTTP 401 for BOTH a whitelist mismatch and an unknown token,
# and distinguishes them only in the response body. Verified live:
#
#   app.bitgo-test.com -> 401 {"error":"Attempt to use IP-restricted token
#                              from an unauthorized IP address"}
#   app.bitgo.com      -> 401 {"error":"No access token"}
#
# Two things follow:
#
# 1. THE TOKEN IS A TEST-ENVIRONMENT TOKEN. Production does not recognise it
#    at all ("No access token"), while test recognised it and objected to the
#    source IP. BitGo's test and production environments hold SEPARATE tokens.
#    So BITGO_ENV=test is correct for this credential.
#
# 2. THE WHITELIST DID NOT MATCH even from the whitelisted host. The most
#    likely cause is IPv6: the host's IPv4 egress is 144.126.133.21 (the
#    whitelisted address), but curl without -4 may leave over IPv6 from a
#    completely different address. Force IPv4 to confirm, and if the host has
#    IPv6 egress either add that address to the token's whitelist or pin the
#    service to IPv4.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
